== Personality ==
Narrator is calm, sarcastic, false factual, and somewhat egotistical. Throughout videos he is frequently the butt of the joke, often being called lame or annoying by MARILLA, or immediately proven wrong of any random belief he has in ''[[The Story of Mobs]]''.

== Abilities ==
Narrator is consistently referred to as simultaneously weak and dangerous, being considered a nuisance to everyone but people worse than him. In one episode, he is described as "physically allergic" to {{MC}}, and causes the sales of any game he mentions to plummet, feats not acknowledged elsewhere.<ref name=":developer">{{YouTube link|MQgWHO_cJp8|The Secrets of Minecraft: Becoming a Game Developer|Minecraft|October 29, 2021}}</ref> He is shown to have musical prowess, capable of playing a harmonica, drum, and a guitar made of mossy cobblestone, as well as over six rap numbers. On multiple occasions he has survived dying or typically lethal situations, including two separate explosions from [[TNT]],<ref name=":survival" /><ref>{{YouTube link|IXu7yKUmBEw|The Secrets of Minecraft: The Allay|Minecraft|March 29, 2022}}</ref> implying he has some form of regenerative ability. 

In his [[Adding a New Mob|first appearance]] he was depicted with the power to create [[Mobbo|entire lifeforms]], but how is never addressed. According to him, when he grows a beard it can "store a lot of food." During an interview, he is described as "[having] somehow already left" the [[Mojang Studios|building]].<ref name=":interview" /> On at least two occasions, he displayed the ability to compress his body into a water cooler, allowing him to evade detection.<ref>{{YouTube link|aBTJIYzJDJw|THE BIOME THAT BROKE MINECRAFT|Minecraft|October 12, 2025}}</ref>

== Biography ==
{{Expand section}}

=== Pre-series ===
Born in approximately 1908,<ref name=":sounds">{{YouTube link|QUfUeHRguPM|The Sounds of Minecraft|Minecraft|October 23, 2020|t=412}} </ref> Narrator is believed to have grown up in a fairly normal life, possessing a teddy bear by the name of Captain Cuddlebuddy.<ref>{{YouTube link|QUfUeHRguPM|The Sounds of Minecraft: How We Make Minecraft - Episode 4|Minecraft|October 23, 2020}}</ref> When he was three years old, he was described as having peaked, and went through a goth phase before he turned middle aged.<ref name=":death">{{YouTube link|n23fRyOfOOg|The Secrets of Minecraft: Death Sounds, Secret Animals, and other Delights!|Minecraft|November 19, 2021}}</ref> In the 1980s, he wore parachute pants, and grew embarrassed of this fact.<ref name=":redstone" /> In 2009, he was on the shortlist for ''{{Wikipedia|Iron Man 2}}''.<ref name=":redstone" /> During his time at "Narration School," he did so poorly in forgery class that he received a grade he referred to as "C++," in actuality an F-. At some point, he took an interest in game modding, and created a mod of {{MC}} called "Minecraft: British Edition."<ref name=":developer" /> For six years, he lived secluded with a family of {{Wikipedia|bears}} in the forest, under assignment of [[Mojang Studios]] to record lines for bears, which ultimately weren't added. At another time, he volunteered to provide the sneezing sound for [[pandas]].<ref name=":death" /> For an unspecified amount of time, he married [[Jonathan Minecraft]], but ended up filing for divorce, claiming it was because of his looks. Jonathan took the house in the process; unbeknownst to him, it was a cardboard fake.<ref name=":survival" />

In 2020, he was given two separate job offerings: take on the role of {{Wikipedia|Iron Man}} in the {{Wikipedia|Marvel Cinematic Universe}}, or provide voiceover for ''Minecraft'', with no compensation beyond [[minecoins]].<ref name=":survival">{{YouTube link|_3s14F5r8bM|Survival: How We Make Minecraft - Episode 6|Minecraft|January 29, 2021}}</ref><ref name=":redstone">{{YouTube link|DLSeGbecKMw|Redstone: How We Make Minecraft - Episode 7|Minecraft|February 26, 2021}}</ref> He ultimately chose the latter, not thinking much of it at the time but growing to regret it.

=== ''How We Make Minecraft'' ===
Narrator first appeared as the host of a show explaining [[How We Make Minecraft|how Mojang makes Minecraft]]. For the first episode, he decided to ease viewers in with the very simple topic of creating life. Using his powers, he brought [[Mobbo]] into existence, which quickly replaced blocks with the [[block of eternal screaming]], and destroyed an entire [[world]].

At some point in 2020, he was sent on assignment into {{MC}} itself to research the habitability of the [[Overworld]].<ref name=":survival" /> Initially he thought that this meant doing a playthrough, claiming he had never played the game prior to that, but it turned out they meant physically transporting him into the game using a [[Machine That Puts Things Into Minecraft|machine]]. Using it, he was seemingly permanently transformed into a [[Character Creator|character]], and sent inside of the game. He awoke on the border of a taiga and plains, and swiftly began searching for resources, trying to chop down a [[spruce]] and [[iron ore]] with a [[raw porkchop]], and creating a small [[farm]]. For whatever reason, the porkchop was discarded into a [[river]]. As the sun set, he sat beneath an [[oak]], and watched out over the [[ocean]].

In order to survive the approaching night, he constructed a small house out of [[dirt]], with a [[spruce door]], and [[grass blocks]] for windowsills. He christened it "MI CASA ES MI CASA," and managed to survive his first night, growing a beard in the process. While he appeared unharmed, he chose to stay indoors the following day, too frightened to leave. He eventually changed his mind, and jumped off a [[cliff]]. From there he was chased and critically injured by a [[skeleton]] during the night, fell into [[lava]] while mining, and died to an inexplicable [[TNT]] block. He carried on, creating a [[carrot]] farm, but his sanity was chipping away.

48 hours into his journey, his hair had grayed and grown exponentially, which caused him to cry alone for several hours. As he left the hut again, he was killed by a [[creeper]]. At another time, he was tricked by a [[sign]] to take a bath in lava, and then tried [[fishing]] in it, where he got told off by a creeper. From there, he somehow managed to acquire a [[diamond pickaxe]] and access to [[the Nether]], where he tried obtaining a [[respawn anchor]]. During this expedition, he constructed a second house made of [[netherrack]], with a [[crimson door]], and [[nylium]] windowsills.

His problems grew worse from there, as he realized he was trapped inside the game. He constructed a large billboard where he spawned, and pretended he had never left his show, giving advice and trivia like he always had. He called out for help in his head, but nobody came. He grew desperate and lonely, spending more time in the game than he'd been alive. After a push he began traveling far beyond his spawn region into a [[cave]], where he kept a journal in case anyone would find him. Under unknown circumstances, he discovered and crawled through a sewer for eight weeks, which somehow freed him from the game.<ref name=":redstone" /> 

At an unknown time, presumably during or after his trek into ''Minecraft'', he was invited to a party by [[Steve]], thinking he would bring [[Jonathan Minecraft]].<ref name=":survival" /> He tried to strike up a conversation with them and [[Alex]] about his beard, but was shunned repeatedly. He then tried to claim the game was realistic.

By February of 2021, he resumed the show like normal. As he started his [[How We Make Minecraft#Redstone|first episode]] back, he made condescending remarks towards Mobbo, not thinking they'd ever get back at him. From there, he attempted to enter a base owned by Steve, and got stuck in a [[piston]] trap. Later in the episode, he suffers a brief mental breakdown. Getting back on track, he decides to build a [[Time Moosheen|time machine]]. During a test, it sets him on fire, but he remains confident it can be used to send him back to 2020. After two more attempts, he reverted to his crazed form, until a piston managed to activate it. Fearing for his life, he was sucked into the portal, and sent to the year 2022, where Mobbo rules the world.

In the episode [[Breaking Minecraft]], he was apparently fired, yet continued showing up to work.<ref>{{YouTube link|IXu7yKUmBEw|The Secrets of Minecraft: The Allay|Minecraft|March 29, 2022}}</ref>

=== ''The Secrets of Minecraft'' ===
At some point, Narrator began working with [[M.A.R.I.L.L.A.]] on a joint venture, providing [[the secrets of Minecraft]]'s development with their own brand of humor.

During his time on the show, he quickly regretted the collaboration, and began seeking out other venues. One day, he tried desperately to get hired at Mojang Studios, and wouldn't leave the [[Villager|staff]] there alone, at one point showing them his mod. After an endorsement of [[Minecraft Education]], he unwittingly jeopardizes the sales of that game, baffling the interviewers.<ref name=":developer" /> Later, his contract was seemingly ripped apart by an unknown figure.<ref name=":death" /><ref>{{YouTube link|cd7cVNeb0Uk|The Secrets of Minecraft: How We're Making the Warden|Minecraft|January 21, 2022}}</ref>

After finishing the first 2,893,000 episodes of the series, Narrator was invited to an interview by [[Tom Stone]].<ref name=":interview" /> During this experience, he reflected on his failed acting career, and bragged about [[How We Make Minecraft|his show]]'s perceived better ratings over [[Ten Things You Probably Didn't Know About Minecraft|M.A.R.I.L.L.A.'s]], before fleeing through unknown means.

He supposedly met his end at the hands of the [[Warden]] by the orders of Mobbo.<ref>{{ytl|Z4haZTbU9ZA|The Secrets of Minecraft's Deep Dark @ 5:14|Minecraft|June 24, 2022|t=67s}}</ref> How he recovered is never addressed.

At an unknown point in time, he and M.A.R.I.L.L.A. did a sponsorship with a fly poison, which apparently works great on [[Steve]].<ref>{{YouTube link|YRPlscod34Y|WOODLAND MANSION MYSTERY: Episode 3|Minecraft|January 6, 2023}}</ref>

